# Build context for backend/Dockerfile, whose context is the repository root rather than
# ./backend. It needs exactly two things: the backend source tree, and the deployed compose
# file that the image carries to the host at /opt/stack/docker-compose.yml.
#
# Written as deny-all-then-admit rather than a list of exclusions. An exclusion list is wrong
# by default: every directory added to this repository afterwards is silently shipped into the
# build context until someone remembers to exclude it. This way a new directory is invisible
# to the build until it is deliberately named here.
#
# Only backend/Dockerfile uses this file. The frontend build's context is ./frontend, and the
# container test tier builds backend/Dockerfile.test with ./backend as its context; Docker
# reads the .dockerignore beside the context root, so neither sees this one.
*

!backend
!ops/deploy/docker-compose.yml

# Re-excluded inside the admitted tree: build residue and local state that must never reach
# an image, and would otherwise invalidate the layer cache on every run.
backend/**/__pycache__
backend/**/*.pyc
backend/**/.pytest_cache
backend/.venv
backend/data
backend/*.db
